Usage: fva explain <project> --spec-module <M> [options]

Explain each claim in plain English, then compare the claims with your requirements.
The requirements file has one "## <id>" line before each requirement. Without a
requirements file, each claim is compared with its author's docstring. The model
explains the claims without their names. The text is saved beside the spec module and
shown again without a model call. A signed-in codex CLI writes the text.

Options:
  --spec-module M    The module that states the claims (required).
  --root-module R    The module that imports the proofs.
  --requirements F   Use the requirements file F (default: requirements.md beside the
                     spec module, when it exists).
  --model M          Use the model M.
  --effort E         Use the reasoning effort E (default medium).
  --force            Write the text again.
  --json             Write the result as JSON.

Exit status: 0 when the trust verdict is PASS, each requirement (or else each claim's
docstring) matches and the saved text is current, 1 otherwise, 2 for a usage error.
